   "conclusion": {
    "diagnosis": "A real anomaly began at the batch 1→batch 2 boundary (around tick 1086): every job 1–9 passed inspection (E12), job 10 passed (E10), then jobs 11, 13 and 15 failed while jobs 12 and 14 passed (E10). Every job runs through all six CNC machines in sequence (CNC-01 … CNC-06) — jobs 11, 12, 13, 14 and 15 all visit every machine (E3, E4, E7, E8) — so no single machine is implicated and a per-machine part replacement is not indicated. The failures alternate by job within batch 2, which fits a batch-boundary configuration/input/per-job condition (H1) rather than a worn component (H2 contradicted by E4/E7/E8) or normal variation (H3 contradicted by E10/E12). Inspections record only pass/fail, so no failure reason is available for jobs 11, 13, 15 (Q6/Q11 unresolved), and the failures are spaced one job apart rather than clustered at shift start/end, so a time-of-day/warm-up effect (Q5/H4) is not supported. Confidence 0.90.",
